From 3adce8545b738fcc2742277e98cf83058031f1ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:30:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] batch: device-to-device slot copy for admissions and slot
 resumes

The main sessions and the batch slot sessions of a stage live on the same device and are
carved alike, so copy_to_slot / copy_from_slot (without a checkpoint) now copy the running
state and the QSA K/V directly (conversation_checkpoint_copy, conversation_kv_copy:
cudaMemcpyAsync on the legacy stream, one device sync before and after) instead of the
checkpoint/K-V image round trip through host memory with a sync per layer. Same bytes into
the same places in the same order; the residency refresh for streamed K/V is shared with
conversation_kv_restore. STRATA_SLOT_COPY_DIRECT=0 restores the host path.

4x RTX 3090, UD-IQ4_XS, --batch 16, split 12,24,36 + --trim-stage-weights: admission copy
65.6 -> 34.0 ms average (pure copy ~8 ms); tools/batch_test16.py 16/16 and
batch_interleave_test.py (incl. next turn from its slot) identical to solo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
